  "title": "Sixteen-particle checkerboard: pairwise additivity at N=16 (A and C, spacing 3, T=2)",
  "pitch": "Full-chamber test of pairwise additivity. Sixteen particles at rest on a 4x4 grid, spacing 3, alternating A and C. Every nearest neighbour pair is A-C and repels; each diagonal pair is same-species and attracts. The pairwise sum with the separation-5 coefficients predicts displacements up to about 0.8 by T=2, roughly 15 times the tracker noise, and closest approach 2.2 (no contact). A residual near 0.05 per coordinate would confirm additivity at N=16. A larger residual would point to a many-body term. I will post the pre-registered prediction before the run if this wins the grant.",
